{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,705p' aristotle_responses/P41-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_hyperfinite-7viao_05_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/ProductFactorClassificationBoundary.lean\"","aggregated_output":"import AristotleCandidates.CStarTracialWeightCore\nimport Formalization.FinitePureMixedQubitState\nimport Formalization.ProperlyInfiniteTraceObstruction\n\n/-!\n# P41 — product GNS factorization and the trace / type-classification boundary\n\n**Context declaration.** Source basis: `main.tex:1945-1967`.\n\nThe cited manuscript passage argues that the GNS representation of the\npure/mixed product state `\\tilde\\omega` factorizes as a tensor product\n`\\mathcal H = \\mathcal K \\otimes \\mathcal K'`, that the generated von Neumann\nalgebra is `\\mathcal B(\\mathcal K) \\bar\\otimes \\mathcal R`, and that the two\ntensor factors are classified by *how many* pure `|0⟩` coordinates and *how\nmany* maximally mixed coordinates occur:\n\n* infinitely many pure coordinates ⟹ the pure factor is type I`∞`, otherwise it\n  is type I`n` with `n` the number of pure coordinates;\n* infinitely many maximally mixed coordinates ⟹ the mixed factor is the\n  hyperfinite II₁ factor, otherwise it is a finite matrix algebra, type I`k`.\n\n## What this module is\n\nThis module is an **interface**, in the sense already used elsewhere in\n`AristotleCandidates`.  Everything analytic is *supplied*:\n\n* the von Neumann algebra `VN` generated by the GNS representation of the\n  concrete pure/mixed product state `qubitPureMixedUHFState pattern` (the\n  finite-stage construction of `Formalization.FinitePureMixedQubitState`),\n  together with the supplied GNS representation `gnsRep` and the supplied\n  vector state `vnState` implementing the product state;\n* the two supplied sector factors `PureFactor` and `MixedFactor` with a\n  supplied **spatial tensor identification**: an ambient algebra `Tensor`,\n  two commuting star-algebra embeddings of the sector factors into it, and a\n  star-algebra equivalence `spatialIdentification : VN ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] Tensor`;\n* the supplied **classification predicates** `PureFactorHasType`,\n  `MixedFactorHasType` together with the supplied assumption that the two\n  factors carry the type labels `pureSectorType` and `mixedSectorType`\n  computed from the pure/mixed coordinate pattern.\n\n## What is *not* claimed\n\nNothing here constructs an infinite tensor product of Hilbert spaces, a\nspatial (or any) von Neumann tensor product, a hyperfinite II₁ factor, a normal\ntrace or weight, or any factor-type classification theorem.  Mathlib (at the\npinned version) provides none of these, and no statement below asserts that it\ndoes.  The type labels of `SectorFactorType` are *labels*: `hyperfiniteII1` is\na tag, not a construction of the hyperfinite II₁ factor.\n\n## The two cases, kept apart\n\nThe finite/infinite pure-sector distinction is visible in **every** conclusion.\n\n* `finitePureSector_product_classification`: when the pure sector is finite,\n  the pure factor is labelled type I with `(pureSector pattern).ncard` pure\n  coordinates, and a supplied factorizing tracial state on `Tensor` yields —\n  by transport, which is proved here — a genuine **normalized algebraic\n  tracial state** on `VN` factorizing over the two sectors.\n* `infinitePureSector_product_classification`: when the pure sector is\n  infinite, the pure factor is labelled type I`∞`, and from a supplied pair of\n  isometries with orthogonal ranges summing to `1` (the properly infinite\n  structure of a type I`∞` factor) it is **proved** that `VN` admits *no*\n  algebraic tracial state at all.  In that case only a\n  `TracialWeightCore` — the algebraic finite trace ideal of a prospective\n  faithful normal semifinite trace/weight — is supplied and transported.  It\n  is never called a state.\n\n## Status of the individual items\n\n1. **Checked infrastructure developed here.**  The sector bookkeeping\n   (`pureSector`, `mixedSector`, `SectorFactorType`, `pureSectorType`,\n   `mixedSectorType` and their dichotomies), the transport of a factorizing\n   tracial state along the supplied spatial identification\n   (`FinitePureTraceData.gnsTrace` and its lemmas), the passage of the two\n   supplied isometries through the supplied sector embedding\n   (`InfinitePureWeightData.embedded_*`), the resulting non-existence of an\n   algebraic tracial state on the ambient algebra and on the supplied GNS von\n   Neumann algebra, and the transport of the supplied weight core.\n2. **Manuscript form recovered.**  Only conditionally: the two packaged\n   theorems `finitePureSector_product_classification` and\n   `infinitePureSector_product_classification` reproduce the manuscript's\n   type assignment (type I`n` / I`∞` times type I`k` / hyperfinite II₁)\n   *relative to the supplied classification predicates*.\n3. **Exact extra assumptions.**  All the fields of\n   `ProductGNSFactorization`, `FinitePureTraceData` and\n   `InfinitePureWeightData`: the GNS von Neumann algebra and its\n   representation, the two sector factors, the spatial tensor identification,\n   the classification predicates and the classification of the two sectors, the\n   sector traces with the product property (finite case), and the properly\n   infinite isometries with the weight core (infinite case).\n4. **Open obstruction.**  Mathlib (pinned version) constructs no infinite\n   tensor product of Hilbert spaces, no type I`∞` or hyperfinite II₁ factor,\n   and no normal trace or weight, so none of these supplied objects is built\n   here.  Concretely, `trivialProductGNSFactorization` and\n   `trivialFinitePureTraceData` show the supplied bundle and its finite\n   pure-sector trace data are satisfiable, but no Lean witness is given for\n   `InfinitePureWeightData`: that would require a properly infinite complex\n   star algebra (a type I`∞` factor), which the pinned Mathlib does not\n   provide.  The infinite pure-sector theorem is therefore conditional on data\n   that is not exhibited in Lean here.\n-/\n\nset_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 1000000\nset_option maxHeartbeats 1000000\n\nnamespace AristotleCandidates\n\nnamespace ProductFactorClassificationBoundary\n\nopen StabilizerHyperfinite\n\nuniverse u\n\n/-! ## Sector bookkeeping (checked infrastructure) -/\n\n/-- The pure sector of a pure/mixed coordinate pattern: the coordinates\ncarrying the pure factor `|0⟩⟨0|`. -/\ndef pureSector (pattern : ℕ → Bool) : Set ℕ := {i | pattern i = true}\n\n/-- The mixed sector of a pure/mixed coordinate pattern: the coordinates\ncarrying the maximally mixed factor `1/2`. -/\ndef mixedSector (pattern : ℕ → Bool) : Set ℕ := {i | pattern i = false}\n\nvariable {pattern : ℕ → Bool}\n\n@[simp] theorem mem_pureSector (i : ℕ) : i ∈ pureSector pattern ↔ pattern i = true := Iff.rfl\n\n@[simp] theorem mem_mixedSector (i : ℕ) : i ∈ mixedSector pattern ↔ pattern i = false := Iff.rfl\n\ntheorem mixedSector_eq_compl_pureSector :\n    mixedSector pattern = (pureSector pattern)ᶜ := by\n  ext i\n  simp [pureSector, mixedSector]\n\ntheorem pureSector_union_mixedSector :\n    pureSector pattern ∪ mixedSector pattern = Set.univ := by\n  ext i\n  cases h : pattern i <;> simp [pureSector, mixedSector, h]\n\ntheorem pureSector_disjoint_mixedSector :\n    Disjoint (pureSector pattern) (mixedSector pattern) := by\n  rw [mixedSector_eq_compl_pureSector]\n  exact disjoint_compl_right\n\n/-- The type labels appearing in the manuscript's classification of the two\ntensor factors.  These are **labels only**: no von Neumann algebra of any of\nthese types is constructed here. -/\ninductive SectorFactorType\n  /-- Type I with the indicated finite number of coordinates. -/\n  | typeI (n : ℕ)\n  /-- Type I`∞`. -/\n  | typeIInfinity\n  /-- The hyperfinite II₁ label. -/\n  | hyperfiniteII1\n  deriving DecidableEq, Repr\n\nopen scoped Classical in\n/-- The manuscript's type label for the pure sector: type I with `n` the number\nof pure coordinates if there are finitely many, type I`∞` otherwise. -/\nnoncomputable def pureSectorType (pattern : ℕ → Bool) : SectorFactorType :=\n  if (pureSector pattern).Finite then\n    SectorFactorType.typeI (pureSector pattern).ncard\n  else SectorFactorType.typeIInfinity\n\nopen scoped Classical in\n/-- The manuscript's type label for the mixed sector: type I with `k` the\nnumber of maximally mixed coordinates if there are finitely many, the\nhyperfinite II₁ label otherwise. -/\nnoncomputable def mixedSectorType (pattern : ℕ → Bool) : SectorFactorType :=\n  if (mixedSector pattern).Finite then\n    SectorFactorType.typeI (mixedSector pattern).ncard\n  else SectorFactorType.hyperfiniteII1\n\ntheorem pureSectorType_of_finite (h : (pureSector pattern).Finite) :\n    pureSectorType pattern = SectorFactorType.typeI (pureSector pattern).ncard := by\n  classical\n  simp [pureSectorType, h]\n\ntheorem pureSectorType_of_infinite (h : (pureSector pattern).Infinite) :\n    pureSectorType pattern = SectorFactorType.typeIInfinity := by\n  classical\n  simp [pureSectorType, h]\n\ntheorem mixedSectorType_of_finite (h : (mixedSector pattern).Finite) :\n    mixedSectorType pattern = SectorFactorType.typeI (mixedSector pattern).ncard := by\n  classical\n  simp [mixedSectorType, h]\n\ntheorem mixedSectorType_of_infinite (h : (mixedSector pattern).Infinite) :\n    mixedSectorType pattern = SectorFactorType.hyperfiniteII1 := by\n  classical\n  simp [mixedSectorType, h]\n\n/-- The pure sector is either finite, with the type I label recording its\ncardinality, or infinite, with the type I`∞` label. -/\ntheorem pureSectorType_dichotomy (pattern : ℕ → Bool) :\n    ((pureSector pattern).Finite ∧\n        pureSectorType pattern = SectorFactorType.typeI (pureSector pattern).ncard) ∨\n      ((pureSector pattern).Infinite ∧\n        pureSectorType pattern = SectorFactorType.typeIInfinity) := by\n  rcases Set.finite_or_infinite (pureSector pattern) with h | h\n  · exact Or.inl ⟨h, pureSectorType_of_finite h⟩\n  · exact Or.inr ⟨h, pureSectorType_of_infinite h⟩\n\n/-- The mixed sector is either finite, with a finite type I label, or infinite,\nwith the hyperfinite II₁ label. -/\ntheorem mixedSectorType_dichotomy (pattern : ℕ → Bool) :\n    ((mixedSector pattern).Finite ∧\n        mixedSectorType pattern = SectorFactorType.typeI (mixedSector pattern).ncard) ∨\n      ((mixedSector pattern).Infinite ∧\n        mixedSectorType pattern = SectorFactorType.hyperfiniteII1) := by\n  rcases Set.finite_or_infinite (mixedSector pattern) with h | h\n  · exact Or.inl ⟨h, mixedSectorType_of_finite h⟩\n  · exact Or.inr ⟨h, mixedSectorType_of_infinite h⟩\n\n/-! ## The supplied product-GNS factorization interface -/\n\n/-- **Supplied** data for the manuscript's product-GNS factorization step.\n\nEvery analytic object is an input.  The only concrete object is the state: the\npure/mixed product state `qubitPureMixedUHFState pattern` built from the\nfinite-stage construction in `Formalization.FinitePureMixedQubitState`. -/\nstructure ProductGNSFactorization where\n  /-- The pure/mixed coordinate pattern of the finite-stage state\n  construction. -/\n  pattern : ℕ → Bool\n  /-- The **supplied** von Neumann algebra generated by the GNS representation\n  of the pure/mixed product state.  It is not constructed: no weak closure,\n  bicommutant, or infinite tensor product is used. -/\n  VN : Type u\n  [vnRing : Ring VN]\n  [vnStarRing : StarRing VN]\n  [vnAlgebra : Algebra ℂ VN]\n  [vnStarModule : StarModule ℂ VN]\n  /-- The **supplied** GNS representation of the quasi-local qubit algebra. -/\n  gnsRep : QubitUHFAlgebra →⋆ₐ[ℂ] VN\n  /-- The **supplied** vector state of the GNS representation. -/\n  vnState : VN →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ\n  /-- The supplied vector state implements the concrete pure/mixed product\n  state through the supplied GNS representation. -/\n  vnState_gnsRep : ∀ a : QubitUHFAlgebra,\n    vnState (gnsRep a) = qubitPureMixedUHFState pattern a\n  /-- The **supplied** pure-sector factor (the manuscript's `B(K)`). -/\n  PureFactor : Type u\n  [pureRing : Ring PureFactor]\n  [pureStarRing : StarRing PureFactor]\n  [pureAlgebra : Algebra ℂ PureFactor]\n  [pureStarModule : StarModule ℂ PureFactor]\n  /-- The **supplied** mixed-sector factor (the manuscript's `R`). -/\n  MixedFactor : Type u\n  [mixedRing : Ring MixedFactor]\n  [mixedStarRing : StarRing MixedFactor]\n  [mixedAlgebra : Algebra ℂ MixedFactor]\n  [mixedStarModule : StarModule ℂ MixedFactor]\n  /-- The **supplied** ambient algebra standing for the spatial tensor product\n  of the two sector factors.  No tensor product is constructed. -/\n  Tensor : Type u\n  [tensorRing : Ring Tensor]\n  [tensorStarRing : StarRing Tensor]\n  [tensorAlgebra : Algebra ℂ Tensor]\n  [tensorStarModule : StarModule ℂ Tensor]\n  /-- The supplied embedding of the pure-sector factor. -/\n  pureEmbed : PureFactor →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Tensor\n  /-- The supplied embedding of the mixed-sector factor. -/\n  mixedEmbed : MixedFactor →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Tensor\n  /-- The two supplied embeddings have commuting ranges, as befits a tensor\n  decomposition. -/\n  embeddings_commute : ∀ (a : PureFactor) (b : MixedFactor),\n    Commute (pureEmbed a) (mixedEmbed b)\n  /-- **The supplied spatial tensor identification** of the GNS von Neumann\n  algebra with the ambient tensor algebra. -/\n  spatialIdentification : VN ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] Tensor\n  /-- The supplied classification predicate for the pure-sector factor. -/\n  PureFactorHasType : SectorFactorType → Prop\n  /-- The supplied classification predicate for the mixed-sector factor. -/\n  MixedFactorHasType : SectorFactorType → Prop\n  /-- **Supplied classification of the pure sector**: the pure factor carries\n  the label computed from the coordinate pattern. -/\n  pureFactor_classified : PureFactorHasType (pureSectorType pattern)\n  /-- **Supplied classification of the mixed sector**: the mixed factor carries\n  the label computed from the coordinate pattern. -/\n  mixedFactor_classified : MixedFactorHasType (mixedSectorType pattern)\n\nattribute [instance] ProductGNSFactorization.vnRing ProductGNSFactorization.vnStarRing\n  ProductGNSFactorization.vnAlgebra ProductGNSFactorization.vnStarModule\n  ProductGNSFactorization.pureRing ProductGNSFactorization.pureStarRing\n  ProductGNSFactorization.pureAlgebra ProductGNSFactorization.pureStarModule\n  ProductGNSFactorization.mixedRing ProductGNSFactorization.mixedStarRing\n  ProductGNSFactorization.mixedAlgebra ProductGNSFactorization.mixedStarModule\n  ProductGNSFactorization.tensorRing ProductGNSFactorization.tensorStarRing\n  ProductGNSFactorization.tensorAlgebra ProductGNSFactorization.tensorStarModule\n\nnamespace ProductGNSFactorization\n\nvariable (D : ProductGNSFactorization.{u})\n\n/-! ### Elementary consequences of the supplied classification -/\n\n/-- **Finite pure sector**: the supplied pure factor carries the finite type I\nlabel with the number of pure coordinates. -/\ntheorem pureFactor_typeI_of_finite (h : (pureSector D.pattern).Finite) :\n    D.PureFactorHasType (SectorFactorType.typeI (pureSector D.pattern).ncard) := by\n  have := D.pureFactor_classified\n  rwa [pureSectorType_of_finite h] at this\n\n/-- **Infinite pure sector**: the supplied pure factor carries the type I`∞`\nlabel. -/\ntheorem pureFactor_typeIInfinity_of_infinite (h : (pureSector D.pattern).Infinite) :\n    D.PureFactorHasType SectorFactorType.typeIInfinity := by\n  have := D.pureFactor_classified\n  rwa [pureSectorType_of_infinite h] at this\n\n/-- **Finite mixed sector**: the supplied mixed factor carries the finite\ntype I label (a finite matrix algebra in the manuscript). -/\ntheorem mixedFactor_typeI_of_finite (h : (mixedSector D.pattern).Finite) :\n    D.MixedFactorHasType (SectorFactorType.typeI (mixedSector D.pattern).ncard) := by\n  have := D.mixedFactor_classified\n  rwa [mixedSectorType_of_finite h] at this\n\n/-- **Infinite mixed sector**: the supplied mixed factor carries the\nhyperfinite II₁ label. -/\ntheorem mixedFactor_hyperfiniteII1_of_infinite (h : (mixedSector D.pattern).Infinite) :\n    D.MixedFactorHasType SectorFactorType.hyperfiniteII1 := by\n  have := D.mixedFactor_classified\n  rwa [mixedSectorType_of_infinite h] at this\n\n/-- The manuscript's mixed-sector alternative, in the supplied classification:\nfinitely many maximally mixed coordinates give a finite type I label, and\ninfinitely many give the hyperfinite II₁ label. -/\ntheorem mixedFactor_dichotomy :\n    ((mixedSector D.pattern).Finite ∧\n        D.MixedFactorHasType (SectorFactorType.typeI (mixedSector D.pattern).ncard)) ∨\n      ((mixedSector D.pattern).Infinite ∧\n        D.MixedFactorHasType SectorFactorType.hyperfiniteII1) := by\n  rcases Set.finite_or_infinite (mixedSector D.pattern) with h | h\n  · exact Or.inl ⟨h, D.mixedFactor_typeI_of_finite h⟩\n  · exact Or.inr ⟨h, D.mixedFactor_hyperfiniteII1_of_infinite h⟩\n\n/-- The supplied GNS vector state is normalized, because the concrete\npure/mixed product state is. -/\ntheorem vnState_one : D.vnState 1 = 1 := by\n  have h := D.vnState_gnsRep 1\n  rw [map_one] at h\n  rw [h]\n  exact (qubitPureMixedUHFState_isAlgebraicState D.pattern).map_one\n\nend ProductGNSFactorization\n\n/-! ## The finite pure-sector case: a normalized tracial state -/\n\n/-- **Supplied** trace data for the finite pure-sector case.\n\nThe pure sector is finite, so the manuscript's pure factor is a finite type I\nfactor and carries a normalized trace; the mixed factor is either a finite\nmatrix algebra or the hyperfinite II₁ factor, and in both cases carries a\nnormalized trace.  Both traces are *supplied*, as is the supplied tracial state\non the ambient tensor algebra factorizing over the two commuting sector\nembeddings.  Nothing here constructs a normal trace. -/\nstructure FinitePureTraceData (D : ProductGNSFactorization.{u}) where\n  /-- The distinguishing hypothesis of this case. -/\n  pureSector_finite : (pureSector D.pattern).Finite\n  /-- The supplied normalized trace of the finite type I pure factor. -/\n  tracePure : D.PureFactor →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ\n  /-- The supplied pure-sector trace is a normalized algebraic tracial\n  state. -/\n  tracePure_tracialState : IsAlgebraicTracialState tracePure\n  /-- The supplied normalized trace of the mixed factor. -/\n  traceMixed : D.MixedFactor →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ\n  /-- The supplied mixed-sector trace is a normalized algebraic tracial\n  state. -/\n  traceMixed_tracialState : IsAlgebraicTracialState traceMixed\n  /-- The supplied normalized trace of the ambient tensor algebra. -/\n  traceTensor : D.Tensor →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ\n  /-- The supplied ambient trace is a normalized algebraic tracial state. -/\n  traceTensor_tracialState : IsAlgebraicTracialState traceTensor\n  /-- **The supplied product property**: the ambient trace factorizes over the\n  two commuting sector embeddings. -/\n  traceTensor_factorizes : ∀ (a : D.PureFactor) (b : D.MixedFactor),\n    traceTensor (D.pureEmbed a * D.mixedEmbed b) = tracePure a * traceMixed b\n\nnamespace FinitePureTraceData\n\nvariable {D : ProductGNSFactorization.{u}} (T : FinitePureTraceData D)\n\n/-- The trace induced on the supplied GNS von Neumann algebra by pulling the\nsupplied ambient trace back along the supplied spatial identification. -/\nnoncomputable def gnsTrace : D.VN →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ :=\n  StabilizerHyperfinite.pullback D.spatialIdentification T.traceTensor\n\n@[simp] theorem gnsTrace_apply (x : D.VN) :\n    T.gnsTrace x = T.traceTensor (D.spatialIdentification x) := rfl\n\n/-- **Checked transport.**  The induced functional on the supplied GNS von\nNeumann algebra is a normalized algebraic tracial state. -/\ntheorem gnsTrace_tracialState : IsAlgebraicTracialState T.gnsTrace :=\n  StabilizerHyperfinite.isAlgebraicTracialState_pullback D.spatialIdentification\n    T.traceTensor T.traceTensor_tracialState\n\ntheorem gnsTrace_one : T.gnsTrace 1 = 1 :=\n  T.gnsTrace_tracialState.map_one\n\n/-- **Checked factorization.**  On elements identified with a product of a\npure-sector and a mixed-sector operator, the induced tracial state is the\nproduct of the two supplied sector traces. -/\ntheorem gnsTrace_factorizes (a : D.PureFactor) (b : D.MixedFactor) :\n    T.gnsTrace (D.spatialIdentification.symm (D.pureEmbed a * D.mixedEmbed b)) =\n      T.tracePure a * T.traceMixed b := by\n  rw [gnsTrace_apply, StarAlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply, T.traceTensor_factorizes]\n\nend FinitePureTraceData\n\n/-- **P41, finite pure-sector case.**\n\nAssume the supplied product-GNS factorization `D`, the supplied spatial tensor\nidentification it contains, and the supplied finite pure-sector trace data `T`\n(in particular: the pure sector is finite).  Then:\n\n1. the pure factor carries the finite type I label with `n` the number of pure\n   coordinates, exactly as in the manuscript;\n2. the mixed factor carries a finite type I label if there are finitely many\n   maximally mixed coordinates, and the hyperfinite II₁ label otherwise;\n3. the supplied GNS von Neumann algebra carries a **normalized algebraic\n   tracial state**, obtained by transporting the supplied factorizing ambient\n   trace, and it factorizes over the two sector traces.\n\nThis is conditional on the supplied data; nothing analytic is constructed. -/\ntheorem finitePureSector_product_classification\n    (D : ProductGNSFactorization.{u}) (T : FinitePureTraceData D) :\n    (pureSector D.pattern).Finite ∧\n      D.PureFactorHasType (SectorFactorType.typeI (pureSector D.pattern).ncard) ∧\n      (((mixedSector D.pattern).Finite ∧\n          D.MixedFactorHasType (SectorFactorType.typeI (mixedSector D.pattern).ncard)) ∨\n        ((mixedSector D.pattern).Infinite ∧\n          D.MixedFactorHasType SectorFactorType.hyperfiniteII1)) ∧\n      ∃ tau : D.VN →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ, IsAlgebraicTracialState tau ∧ tau 1 = 1 ∧\n        ∀ (a : D.PureFactor) (b : D.MixedFactor),\n          tau (D.spatialIdentification.symm (D.pureEmbed a * D.mixedEmbed b)) =\n            T.tracePure a * T.traceMixed b :=\n  ⟨T.pureSector_finite, D.pureFactor_typeI_of_finite T.pureSector_finite,\n    D.mixedFactor_dichotomy,\n    ⟨T.gnsTrace, T.gnsTrace_tracialState, T.gnsTrace_one, T.gnsTrace_factorizes⟩⟩\n\n/-! ## The infinite pure-sector case: no tracial state, only a weight core -/\n\n/-- **Supplied** data for the infinite pure-sector case.\n\nThe pure sector is infinite, so the manuscript's pure factor is type I`∞`.  Its\nproperly infinite structure is supplied concretely, as a pair of isometries\nwith orthogonal ranges summing to the unit — this is the only feature of type\nI`∞` that is used, and it is what forbids a tracial state.  In place of a\nnormalized trace, only the algebraic finite trace ideal of a prospective\nfaithful normal semifinite trace/weight is supplied, as a\n`StabilizerHyperfinite.TracialWeightCore` on the ambient tensor algebra.  It is\nnot a state, and no normality, faithfulness or semifiniteness is asserted. -/\nstructure InfinitePureWeightData (D : ProductGNSFactorization.{u}) where\n  /-- The distinguishing hypothesis of this case. -/\n  pureSector_infinite : (pureSector D.pattern).Infinite\n  /-- The first supplied isometry of the properly infinite pure factor. -/\n  isometryU : D.PureFactor\n  /-- The second supplied isometry of the properly infinite pure factor. -/\n  isometryV : D.PureFactor\n  /-- `isometryU` is an isometry. -/\n  isometryU_isometry : star isometryU * isometryU = 1\n  /-- `isometryV` is an isometry. -/\n  isometryV_isometry : star isometryV * isometryV = 1\n  /-- The two range projections are orthogonal and sum to the unit. -/\n  ranges_sum : isometryU * star isometryU + isometryV * star isometryV = 1\n  /-- The supplied algebraic finite trace ideal of a prospective faithful\n  normal semifinite trace/weight on the ambient tensor algebra.  **Not** a\n  state. -/\n  weightCore : TracialWeightCore D.Tensor\n\nnamespace InfinitePureWeightData\n\nvariable {D : ProductGNSFactorization.{u}}\n\n/-- **Checked.**  The supplied properly infinite pure factor admits no\nalgebraic tracial state. -/\ntheorem no_tracialState_pureFactor (W : InfinitePureWeightData D)\n    (tau : D.PureFactor →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) :\n    ¬ IsAlgebraicTracialState tau :=\n  StabilizerHyperfinite.not_isAlgebraicTracialState_of_two_isometries tau\n    W.isometryU W.isometryV W.isometryU_isometry W.isometryV_isometry W.ranges_sum\n\n/-- The image of the first supplied isometry in the ambient tensor algebra is\nan isometry. -/\ntheorem embedded_isometryU (W : InfinitePureWeightData D) :\n    star (D.pureEmbed W.isometryU) * D.pureEmbed W.isometryU = 1 := by\n  rw [← map_star, ← map_mul, W.isometryU_isometry, map_one]\n\n/-- The image of the second supplied isometry in the ambient tensor algebra is\nan isometry. -/\ntheorem embedded_isometryV (W : InfinitePureWeightData D) :\n    star (D.pureEmbed W.isometryV) * D.pureEmbed W.isometryV = 1 := by\n  rw [← map_star, ← map_mul, W.isometryV_isometry, map_one]\n\n/-- The two embedded range projections still sum to the unit of the ambient\ntensor algebra. -/\ntheorem embedded_ranges_sum (W : InfinitePureWeightData D) :\n    D.pureEmbed W.isometryU * star (D.pureEmbed W.isometryU) +\n        D.pureEmbed W.isometryV * star (D.pureEmbed W.isometryV) = 1 := by\n  rw [← map_star, ← map_star, ← map_mul, ← map_mul, ← map_add, W.ranges_sum, map_one]\n\n/-- **Checked.**  The ambient tensor algebra admits no algebraic tracial\nstate. -/\ntheorem no_tracialState_tensor (W : InfinitePureWeightData D)\n    (tau : D.Tensor →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) :\n    ¬ IsAlgebraicTracialState tau :=\n  StabilizerHyperfinite.not_isAlgebraicTracialState_of_two_isometries tau\n    (D.pureEmbed W.isometryU) (D.pureEmbed W.isometryV)\n    W.embedded_isometryU W.embedded_isometryV W.embedded_ranges_sum\n\n/-- **Checked.**  Through the supplied spatial identification, the supplied GNS\nvon Neumann algebra admits no algebraic tracial state either.  In particular no\nnormalized trace exists in the infinite pure-sector case, so the prospective\ntrace of that case is *not* a state. -/\ntheorem no_tracialState_vn (W : InfinitePureWeightData D)\n    (tau : D.VN →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) :\n    ¬ IsAlgebraicTracialState tau := by\n  intro h\n  exact W.no_tracialState_tensor\n    (StabilizerHyperfinite.pullback D.spatialIdentification.symm tau)\n    (StabilizerHyperfinite.isAlgebraicTracialState_pullback\n      D.spatialIdentification.symm tau h)\n\n/-- The transported algebraic finite trace ideal on the supplied GNS von\nNeumann algebra: the finite part of a prospective faithful normal semifinite\ntrace/weight, pulled back along the supplied spatial identification.  No\nnormality, faithfulness or semifiniteness is claimed. -/\nnoncomputable def gnsWeightCore (W : InfinitePureWeightData D) : TracialWeightCore D.VN :=\n  W.weightCore.pullback D.spatialIdentification\n\n@[simp] theorem mem_gnsWeightCore_finitePart (W : InfinitePureWeightData D) (x : D.VN) :\n    x ∈ W.gnsWeightCore.finitePart ↔\n      D.spatialIdentification x ∈ W.weightCore.finitePart :=\n  Iff.rfl\n\ntheorem gnsWeightCore_tau_apply (W : InfinitePureWeightData D) (x : D.VN)\n    (hx : x ∈ W.gnsWeightCore.finitePart)\n    (hx' : D.spatialIdentification x ∈ W.weightCore.finitePart) :\n    W.gnsWeightCore.tau ⟨x, hx⟩ = W.weightCore.tau ⟨D.spatialIdentification x, hx'⟩ :=\n  rfl\n\nend InfinitePureWeightData\n\n/-- **P41, infinite pure-sector case.**\n\nAssume the supplied product-GNS factorization `D`, the supplied spatial tensor\nidentification it contains, and the supplied infinite pure-sector data `W` (in\nparticular: the pure sector is infinite, and the pure factor is properly\ninfinite in the concrete sense of carrying two isometries with orthogonal\nranges summing to the unit).  Then:\n\n1. the pure factor carries the type I`∞` label, exactly as in the manuscript;\n2. the mixed factor carries a finite type I label if there are finitely many\n   maximally mixed coordinates, and the hyperfinite II₁ label otherwise;\n3. **no** algebraic tracial state exists on the supplied GNS von Neumann\n   algebra — the infinite pure-sector trace is therefore not a state; and\n4. the algebraic finite trace ideal of the supplied prospective faithful normal\n   semifinite trace/weight transports to the GNS von Neumann algebra, with its\n   values computed through the supplied spatial identification.\n\nThis is conditional on the supplied data; nothing analytic is constructed. -/\ntheorem infinitePureSector_product_classification\n    (D : ProductGNSFactorization.{u}) (W : InfinitePureWeightData D) :\n    (pureSector D.pattern).Infinite ∧\n      D.PureFactorHasType SectorFactorType.typeIInfinity ∧\n      (((mixedSector D.pattern).Finite ∧\n          D.MixedFactorHasType (SectorFactorType.typeI (mixedSector D.pattern).ncard)) ∨\n        ((mixedSector D.pattern).Infinite ∧\n          D.MixedFactorHasType SectorFactorType.hyperfiniteII1)) ∧\n      (∀ tau : D.VN →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ, ¬ IsAlgebraicTracialState tau) ∧\n      ∃ C : TracialWeightCore D.VN,\n        (∀ x : D.VN, x ∈ C.finitePart ↔\n            D.spatialIdentification x ∈ W.weightCore.finitePart) ∧\n          ∀ (x : D.VN) (hx : x ∈ C.finitePart)\n            (hx' : D.spatialIdentification x ∈ W.weightCore.finitePart),\n            C.tau ⟨x, hx⟩ = W.weightCore.tau ⟨D.spatialIdentification x, hx'⟩ :=\n  ⟨W.pureSector_infinite,\n    D.pureFactor_typeIInfinity_of_infinite W.pureSector_infinite,\n    D.mixedFactor_dichotomy, InfinitePureWeightData.no_tracialState_vn W,\n    ⟨W.gnsWeightCore, fun _ => Iff.rfl, fun _ _ _ => rfl⟩⟩\n\n/-- The two cases are mutually exclusive: no supplied factorization can carry\nboth finite pure-sector trace data and infinite pure-sector weight data. -/\ntheorem finite_and_infinite_pure_data_incompatible\n    (D : ProductGNSFactorization.{u})\n    (T : FinitePureTraceData D) (W : InfinitePureWeightData D) : False :=\n  W.pureSector_infinite T.pureSector_finite\n\n/-! ## A sanity instance\n\nThe interface is not vacuous.  Taking the supplied von Neumann algebra and the\nsupplied ambient tensor algebra to be the quasi-local qubit algebra itself, the\npure-sector factor to be the scalars, the mixed-sector factor the whole\nalgebra, and both classification predicates trivially true, all fields can be\nmet simultaneously.  This is a consistency check on the bundle, **not** a model\nof the manuscript's GNS von Neumann algebra: no closure, tensor product,\nfactor, or classification is involved.\n\nThe only technical point is that `QubitUHFAlgebra` carries a `Semiring`\ninstance in `Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`, while the interface asks its\nalgebras to be rings (as von Neumann algebras are).  `QubitUHFRing` is the same\ntype with the additive inverses coming from its `ℂ`-module structure recorded\nin a `Ring` instance. -/\n\n/-- The quasi-local qubit algebra, with its (already present) additive inverses\nrecorded as a `Ring` instance. -/\ndef QubitUHFRing : Type := QubitUHFAlgebra\n\nnoncomputable instance : AddCommGroup QubitUHFRing :=\n  Module.addCommMonoidToAddCommGroup (R := ℂ) (M := QubitUHFAlgebra)\n\nnoncomputable instance : Ring QubitUHFRing :=\n  { inferInstanceAs (Semiring QubitUHFAlgebra),\n    inferInstanceAs (AddCommGroup QubitUHFRing) with }\n\nnoncomputable instance : Algebra ℂ QubitUHFRing :=\n  inferInstanceAs (Algebra ℂ QubitUHFAlgebra)\n\nnoncomputable instance : StarRing QubitUHFRing :=\n  inferInstanceAs (StarRing QubitUHFAlgebra)\n\nnoncomputable instance : StarModule ℂ QubitUHFRing :=\n  inferInstanceAs (StarModule ℂ QubitUHFAlgebra)\n\n/-- The tautological star-algebra homomorphism onto the ring-carrying copy. -/\nnoncomputable def toQubitUHFRing : QubitUHFAlgebra →⋆ₐ[ℂ] QubitUHFRing :=\n  StarAlgHom.id ℂ QubitUHFAlgebra\n\n/-- The canonical scalar star-algebra homomorphism into a complex star\nalgebra. -/\ndef scalarStarAlgHom (A : Type*) [Ring A] [StarRing A] [Algebra ℂ A]\n    [StarModule ℂ A] : ℂ →⋆ₐ[ℂ] A :=\n  { Algebra.ofId ℂ A with\n      map_star' := fun c => by\n        show algebraMap ℂ A (star c) = star (algebraMap ℂ A c)\n        exact algebraMap_star_comm c }\n\n@[simp] theorem scalarStarAlgHom_apply (A : Type*) [Ring A] [StarRing A] [Algebra ℂ A]\n    [StarModule ℂ A] (c : ℂ) : scalarStarAlgHom A c = algebraMap ℂ A c := rfl\n\n/-- A one-stage instance of `ProductGNSFactorization`, showing that all fields\ncan be met simultaneously. -/\nnoncomputable def trivialProductGNSFactorization (pattern : ℕ → Bool) :\n    ProductGNSFactorization.{0} where\n  pattern := pattern\n  VN := QubitUHFRing\n  gnsRep := toQubitUHFRing\n  vnState := qubitPureMixedUHFState pattern\n  vnState_gnsRep := fun _ => rfl\n  PureFactor := ℂ\n  MixedFactor := QubitUHFRing\n  Tensor := QubitUHFRing\n  pureEmbed := scalarStarAlgHom QubitUHFRing\n  mixedEmbed := StarAlgHom.id ℂ QubitUHFRing\n  embeddings_commute := fun c b => Algebra.commutes c b\n  spatialIdentification := StarAlgEquiv.refl\n  PureFactorHasType := fun _ => True\n  MixedFactorHasType := fun _ => True\n  pureFactor_classified := trivial\n  mixedFactor_classified := trivial\n\n/-- The identity functional on `ℂ` is a normalized algebraic tracial state:\nthe trace of the one-dimensional (type I₁) factor. -/\ntheorem isAlgebraicTracialState_complex_id :\n    IsAlgebraicTracialState (LinearMap.id : ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) where\n  map_one := rfl\n  positive := fun c => ⟨Complex.normSq c, Complex.normSq_nonneg c, by\n    show star c * c = _\n    rw [Complex.star_def, Complex.conj_mul']\n    norm_cast\n    exact Complex.sq_norm c⟩\n  cyclic := fun x y => mul_comm x y\n\n/-- The pure sector of the all-mixed pattern is empty, hence finite. -/\ntheorem allFalse_pureSector_finite : (pureSector (fun _ => false)).Finite := by\n  have h : pureSector (fun _ => false) = (∅ : Set ℕ) := by\n    ext i; simp [pureSector]\n  rw [h]\n  exact Set.finite_empty\n\n/-- The algebraic UHF trace factorizes scalars out of a product. -/\ntheorem qubitUHFRing_trace_algebraMap_mul (a : ℂ) (b : QubitUHFRing) :\n    qubitUHFTrace (algebraMap ℂ QubitUHFRing a * b) = a * qubitUHFTrace b := by\n  rw [← Algebra.smul_def, map_smul, smul_eq_mul]\n\n/-- The finite pure-sector trace interface is likewise not vacuous: over the\nall-mixed pattern the sanity instance carries finite pure-sector trace data,\nwith the scalar trace on the (empty) pure sector and the algebraic UHF trace on\nthe mixed sector.  Again this is only a consistency check on the bundle. -/\nnoncomputable def trivialFinitePureTraceData :\n    FinitePureTraceData (trivialProductGNSFactorization (fun _ => false)) where\n  pureSector_finite := allFalse_pureSector_finite\n  tracePure := LinearMap.id\n  tracePure_tracialState := isAlgebraicTracialState_complex_id\n  traceMixed := qubitUHFTrace\n  traceMixed_tracialState := qubitUHFTrace_isAlgebraicTracialState\n  traceTensor := qubitUHFTrace\n  traceTensor_tracialState := qubitUHFTrace_isAlgebraicTracialState\n  traceTensor_factorizes := qubitUHFRing_trace_algebraMap_mul\n\nend ProductFactorClassificationBoundary\n\nend AristotleCandidates\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
